lines+=['','The independent x86_64 GitHub allocation is distinct from the local arm64 Docker VM. No pooled machine comparison, hardware exclusivity, cold-cache or power-loss qualification is claimed. Build protocols, logs, source manifests, all paired samples and traces are retained.','','## Incomplete mixed matrix','','[Run 39962691064](https://github.com/nowledge-co/hawdb/actions/runs/39962691064) used the same revisions, explicit writers 1/4/8 and readers 0/W/2W over both profiles. Its two physical cores/four logical CPUs selected one writer automatically; larger explicit counts are oversubscribed overrides, not proof of CPU-parallel mutation. Only post-checkpoint 1W/0R and 1W/1R finished. Candidate 1W/2R measured pair 19 exited 101 on `writes_during_reads > 0 && reads_during_writes > 0`. The raw failure and partial samples are retained. This is missing mixed-overlap coverage, not an observed row/epoch mismatch; the full 18-cohort matrix did not complete. No concurrency assertion was removed and the measurement was not retried. A failed artifact download was retried without rerunning the workload.','','## Consumer controls and sustained workload','','The clean-main control used three rounds, two document shapes (32 x 128 B and 512 x 1,024 B), writers 1/4/8, and disabled/scoped-blocking/detached modes: 54 cases, 4,096 foreground writes and the original fixed 16 maintenance triggers in every case. Enabled modes perform 16 successful publications plus 32 quiet publications. Exact source epochs, foreground rows and every document passed. Only one of 18 detached cases and five of 18 scoped cases met repeated post-E progress; quiet timing is not simultaneous progress.','','The local Linux arm64 VM had a four-CPU container quota and 6 GiB memory/swap ceiling. It used the pinned Rust image, Rust 1.97.1, default features and the unmodified global optimized bench profile. Fresh clean-main compilation took 6m 37s; the two-benchmark prototype rebuild took 9m 36s with existing caches. Container wall time also includes toolchain-component acquisition. Source `Auto` residency is not resolved in the record; 512 MiB source-governor configuration is not a whole-process or checkpoint-heap claim. Callback timing is a lower bound on outer-owner residency, not inner selector-lock instrumentation.','','The first separately declared 100,000-write cohort, without checkpoints, failed before WAL append at 100,001 live overlay entries against the production 100,000-entry limit. That is a retained fail-closed resource refusal. Its fixture is preserved; neither the live-row ceiling nor the 64 MiB retention-byte cap was raised.','','The new sustained prototype keeps 100,000 writes, performs normal checkpoints every 16,384 foreground commits and publishes until writers drain or 4,096 attempts. The entry reservation includes the maximum trigger count. Its full predeclared workload is 18 cases, not a shorter favorable sample. Five cases completed with six checkpoints each and repeated post-E publication; case six (512 documents, eight writers) returned `Feed(Incomplete)` at complete-source verification. The helper has a fixed 100,000-advance loop without a separate completion assertion; loop exhaustion is the source-based explanation, not a captured step-counter measurement. Incomplete staging remains rejected. No step budget, production limit, durability policy or acceptance assertion was relaxed. This partial cohort does not establish sustained acceptance.','','Minimal interface proofs (64 writes and 20,000 checkpointed writes) are labelled correctness-only and cannot replace the full cohort or strict performance gate. The five-case partial run and failed fixtures are retained. The later 54-case prototype controls are an independent same-binary experiment, not a retry of the sustained failure.','','## WAL admission and syscall attribution','','The original writer trace identified 31/33 `statx` calls per durable ungrouped/grouped commit on writer threads. Admission enumerated retained-generation files even when its pressure result was discarded on permitted writes. The prototype evaluates a conservative `u64::MAX` retained-generation debt first; if even that permits mutation, exact inventory cannot make permission more restrictive. Refusals reevaluate actual bytes and preserve complete diagnostics. Public pressure reports, namespace fencing, available-space observations and WAL barriers remain unchanged.','','Two storage-unit regressions check that permitted admission does not observe inventory and compare exact refusal snapshots over 1,536 pressure states. These tests belong to existing CI owners; compilation is not runtime test qualification. Trace results are work attribution only; traced latency is excluded. Whole-process extra `fsync` counts include setup, checkpoint, artifact publication and cleanup. The original writer threads had 256 `fdatasync` calls and one `fsync` each; extra whole-process `fsync` must not be described as a per-commit regression.','','## Reproduction and artifact integrity','','Use the checked-in manual drivers and the retained command/protocol files. `*.gz` files are lossless gzip with their original JSON/JSONL/log contents; `raw-artifact-index.json` records compressed and original hashes and sizes. Executable SHA-256 values are retained, while database fixtures and executable binaries are excluded from this repository evidence. Failed fixtures remain in the local named fixture volumes. No new scheduled/default CI benchmark job is added. Historical datasets remain linked from the existing qualification reports.']
(out/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
